+// Explicit gc.collect() does one short slice and returns. The VM hook keeps
+// going until the mark is closed and the sweep finishes. A Dijkstra barrier
+// (shade the newly stored pointer) lets the mutator run during the mark.
+// Allocations during the sweep are born marked when the sweeper has not
+// reached them yet, so they are not treated as garbage.
+//
+// gc_alloc's threshold and out-of-memory paths call gc_collect_full_now()
+// and still run the cycle to the end. That is what the gcamt "fire=yes"
+// duration measures.
